Subject: [PATCH] fcgi: relax automake GNU file requirements

The legacy FastCGI source tree does not ship NEWS, AUTHORS and ChangeLog.
Newer automake used by Yocto 2.5.1 treats the project as GNU-style and
fails during autoreconf when those files are missing.

Mark the project as "foreign" so automake does not require the standard
GNU documentation files.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [legacy source compatibility]
---
 Makefile.am | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/Makefile.am
+++ b/Makefile.am
@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@
+AUTOMAKE_OPTIONS = foreign
+
-- 
